                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/265: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Burdett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-27T11:00:00-03:00">November 27, 1940—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>612. For the Under Secretary. Reference my telegram No. 607, November 26, 5 p.m.
                    The Lloyd Brasiliera local company operating the ship has just received a
                    telegram from the master saying that the ship is being taken to England.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Burdett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
